A||N||26||kupop87gt||Exhaust Systems||||5||
Z||000000||kupop87gt||02-06-2000||03:20 AM||||Hi, I was wondering what you all are doing for an exhaust system. I'm going to get one fairly soon now, but I'm finding my options are fairly low. I had wanted Stainless Steel, but I've only found two systems of the sort available-one of which the dealer isn't even recommending! The other? Fairly expensive. I've considered settling with the Ocelot from the Fiero Store, which is alluminized. Just wondering what your experiences are. Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||02-06-2000||06:38 AM||||I got the Ocelot from the Fiero Store back in June and I'm very happy with it so far. It's not a high flow system or anything that might increase hp but I noticed a difference about 2 weeks after I got it when it seemed like it "broke itself in"! ||||reg||14
Z||000002||stimpy||02-06-2000||08:49 AM||||What kind of system is the dealer not recommending?  I use a Flowmaster and low restriction cat w/ 3" pipe. It is not  an off the shelf system, nor was it cheap.  But it does sound great and really gives some low end spark.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||02-06-2000||11:09 AM||||I gutted my cat and it sounds 10X better then before.<P>Of course it had a bad exhaust manifold gasket and there was a huge hole right behind the cat.  But people teel me it sounds like a small V8.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||02-06-2000||06:03 PM||||There was a thread last month on stainless steel exhaust systems - specifically the BORLA system...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002112.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002112.html</A> <P>||||reg||10
Z||000005||kupop87gt||02-06-2000||08:21 PM||||Thanks for the responses, I'm looking into getting the Borla system from Fiero Parts and Appraisals. The price is right, I was wondering how easy a cat-back system is to install. This would be my first time, so I'm not exactly sure what is involved.<BR> Though, if getting the Borla unit doesn't workout-I was wondering relatively how long the Ocelot (aluminized) unit should last.<BR>Thanks.||||reg||7
Z||000006||stimpy||02-06-2000||10:37 PM||||A cat-back system should be pretty easy money. And the Borla system shore do look purty in them pikshures. Have yet to see one in real life.  How many miles is on your current system?  If it is high miles, you may want to replace your catalytic converter as well.  As the mileage gets up there, the cat gets less efficient and more restrictive.  Newer generation cats are very low restriction.<BR> <BR>Related Q. Since putting my lower restriction exhaust on, I have had an issue with my check engine ight coming on at idle. Checked codes, O2 sensor.  New O2 sensor installed, still getting light. Could this be due to lower density of exhaust gases? Anyone else have experience with that? Any physicist in da house? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||kupop87gt||02-06-2000||11:46 PM||||The cc is actually fairly new. I bought the car last July and haven't run it much. The previous owner said he had "just replaced it" although, he hadn't run the car in forever. The cat's fine though. 88k miles.<BR>I am FAR from a physiscist, lol.<BR>(A note about previous owner though. He was so lazy, he changed only the rear spark-plugs while he left the firewall-side plugs in for god-knows how long. That's always nice to know!)||||reg||10
Z||000008||jlhuber||02-06-2000||11:55 PM||||where is everyone getting their low-restrict. cats from?  i am in need of a system and i'm going with the borla, but i need to replace my cat too.  all i can find so far is the factory replacement cat.  any help is grateful.  TIA||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||02-07-2000||12:44 AM||||Stimpy, what's the code? I don't see where the change in exhaust would throw a code. The EGR test is not that sophisticated.<P>Also, I'm curious what you folks are calling "high flow"? What's the rating for this. Under 5 PSI? Under 10 PSI? I measured my stock V6 at WOT (high load) and it never went over 2 PSI. The manual states 1.25PSI at 2500 with no load is normal.  <P>I guess I'm saying that the assumption that factory systems have high backpressure is not always a good one.<P>Replace it for sound? Sure. Replace it for backpressure? Measure it first. A 0-10 PSI gauge adapted to a gutted O2 sensor works good. If it's under 3 PSI at WOT (driving, not standing still), it's already high flow. Every high flow cat I've seen is no different than a good cat. Lousy cats and mufflers can cause high backpressure.  <P>I'm not try to start a flame war, I'm just curious.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||geyser||02-07-2000||01:06 AM||||So if I gut the cat, how will it affect the smog tests, or for that matter the ECM?||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||02-07-2000||11:15 PM||||The ECM won't care. You very well might fail HC.||||reg||1
Z||000012||86SE||02-07-2000||11:45 PM||||How do V-6 Fieros sound with NO cat??  Mines got a hole it in (somewhere) and sounds like chyt!!  So i'm going to cut it out and put some 2.5" pipe in its place.....Will it sound cool??||||reg||10
Z||000013||Phaeton||02-08-2000||12:00 AM||||My cat plugged up and got replaced by a length of tubing buttwelded where the cat was.  It really brought out the low notes, almost to the point of annoyance.  My milage went up but thats because I try real real hard to keep the rpm's low when just putting around, the burbles start after 2k, but it sounds Fine at WOT without being blatant, it is still a factory silencer.||||reg||1
Z||000014||FIEROCIOUS||02-08-2000||01:26 AM||||In reply to: Why the O2 code at Idle.<BR>More than likely your exhaust is being deluted. The computer expects a certain amount of oxygen at X amount of RPM,temp,throttle position. Thus a speed densidy system. After the car is warm if you have a "Air leak" before the O2 sensor this expected amount is "deluted" causeing the computer to go (What the funk!) I've even seen the O2 sensor loose in the socket or the connection bad to cause the same symptom.||||reg||3
Z||000015||Standard||02-08-2000||01:34 AM||||My 86.5 GT has no cat, and it sounds sweet.  Need to get my front manifold fixed so I can really hear what it sounds like, but standing about 5 feet behind it it purrs, loudly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Remember, loud pipes save lives!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><B>Disclaimer</B>:<BR>Results may vary if you're old.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||penetrator||02-08-2000||08:45 AM||||For 86SE:<P>Go to <A HREF="http://www.hyperwerks.se/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.hyperwerks.se/fiero/</A>  if you want to listen to a Fiero V6 without the Cat, and with Fierostore sprint headers. there is 2 samples(sounds) one in the main page, and one in the "other locations". They will automaticly load, so you dont need to download manually. It might take a while if you are using a modem, but its worth is.<P>=)||||reg||10
Z||000017||Monkeyman||02-08-2000||09:08 AM||||Are those the only modifications to the exhaust?  That sounds nice.||||reg||1
Z||000018||penetrator||02-08-2000||09:14 AM||||Yes, it is. <P>But i also have drilled up the intakehole on the side (The plastic thing inside) and got a ADS superchip.<BR>Almost forgot the resonated ANSA tips, but its sounded similar without the ANSA tips.||||reg||1
Z||000019||superXmotorsports||02-08-2000||06:50 PM||||I've used/tried every exhaust combo out there.  I found the Ocelot to be too restrictive and had a bad resonation at 3,000 RPM's.  The Borla system was nice and free-flowing but too quiet (and $$).<BR>I would like to try the B&B triflow system from Fiero Heaven next.  It includes a high-flow cat and bolts directly to the factory downpipe.  The entire system is polished and looks good.  SXM.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Capt Fiero||02-08-2000||08:01 PM||||I have heard of alot of people using the 82-92 Camero Muffler on a Fiere becuase it is the same muffler at half the price you can get almost anybrand that you want, from what I hear the only mod you have to do is add the little hooks for your springs to mount too.  A quick tack weld at most shops should not be more than a few bucks.  With the Fiero muffler being 200-1200$ depending on system I think that a 40 Flowmaster is a good idea to look into.  The Camero has the proper 1 in and 2 out for the Fiero, it is essentally the same muffler, you got to hand it to GM for using off the shelf parts and then just not telling anyone what car they came off of.||||reg||1
Z||000021||WKDFIRO||02-08-2000||09:42 PM||||First off FOCOA now has the exact replacement muffler for (I think) $70. It just came out of the last magazine and mine is at work. <P>Plus I have heard unsubstantiated reports that Flowmaster has come out with a smaller muffler that fits Fieros and that is slightly quieter because of chamber techniques.<P>I am planning hopefully this month to go to my friendly neighborhood muffler shop and flange the cat and fit a "test pipe," go 2.5 inch exhaust from the catback have him split it off straight to the Megs chrome 4.5 inch wide exhaust tips with fiberglass baffles. This way if I want to go to the track, off comes the cat, out goes the baffles and Im running straight pipe baby! Gotta be cool? Cat goes back on baffles stay put and I still sound mean if I want to but more subtle. Will no muffler work? Dunno, I'll find out next month.||||reg||6
Z||000022||Monkeyman||02-08-2000||09:53 PM||||SXM--Can you give us some info on your straight through exhaust system?  I forget the name, but it seemed like a good idea when I 1st heard of it.  What about resonators for it?||||reg||1
Z||000023||superXmotorsports||02-08-2000||10:02 PM||||MM you can run resonated tips (I always ran 4.5" Megs) or if you're not worried about the cat you can run a 'pre' muffler (I was going to use a titanium one on the speedster) and do it that way.  It sounds awesome but too loud for some!  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Alex4mula||02-09-2000||11:39 AM||||I once had the muffler eliminator that the Fiero Store used to sell (maybe still), without cat and with resonator tips. It did a difference but it was way too loud for everyday use. After it rusted I was happy to put back my original muffler. What is the cost of the system sold by Fiero heaven? Do they have a web page? Where can I find more info on them? Tks. ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Monkeyman||02-09-2000||08:33 PM||||SXM--I don't care about a cat or a muffler.  What is a "pre-muffler" any way?  I was under the impression that your system was basically straight pipes except that they weren't actually straight.||||reg||1
Z||000026||1FST2M6||02-10-2000||08:30 AM||||High Flow or Low restriction cats are available at <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  their cheaper than buying them from Random Technologys and the same thing... I'm running a 2.5" unit and love ever minute of it.. passes emissions and turns mid 13s!||||reg||1
